l all day long this looks awesome i  love that we're taking some shortcuts  here with the pancake mix and the frozen  seafood and the salad greens and the  acorn jelly because i don't know i  looked up a recipe for that acorn jelly  and that is intense store-bought i can  do but we are getting lots of protein  from the seafood we got fiber in the  side salad as well as some fats from the  sesame oil and some seeds and i had  never heard of acorn jelly before but it  is apparently sodium free has a bit of  fiber and has only 40 calories per  serving so definitely something to check  out the next time i'm at the market yes  again this is a high sodium meal mainly  because the girl gets pretty generous on  the soy sauce on her greens i mean hey  if she likes it and it doesn't bother  her then i get the sense that she knows  her body's needs well some of us myself  included actually just need a little  extra salt but if you are sensitive and  you want to make a salad like this at  home you could swap out the soy for a  rice wine vinegar and then season with a  hint of salt or soy  it's brown sugar bubble milk tea cream  bar  i'm so so full right now but  there's always room for dessert brown  sugar bubble tea ice cream sounds fire  and i don't normally like bubble tea but  if it's brown sugar i'm there and while  michelle does comment on how full she  feels i think it's worth distinguishing  between the different types of hunger  all of which are valid reasons to eat so  of course we've got stomach hunger which  is the physical sensation of hunger  which is usually signaled by physical  cues like a grumbling stomach or our  stomach feeling physically full after a  meal then there is mouth hunger which  has more to do with the senses so it  could be a craving for a particular  aspect of food like sweet or crunchy or  salty so michelle's comment that she was  full but she could always find room for  dessert is an example of that mouth  hunger and we've all felt that need 